sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant AE as A Edge
    participant K as KMS/HSM
    participant CP as Policy/Key Auth
    participant BG as B Gateway
    participant AU as Audit
    AE->>K: create per-package DEK
    K-->>AE: transient DEK handle
    AE->>AE: AES-256-GCM encrypt DICOM/chunks
    AE->>K: wrap for device + escrow (package,manifest hash)
    K-->>AE: Key Envelope refs; raw DEK not persisted
    BG->>CP: request release(consent,Ticket,B,Study,device,integrity)
    CP->>CP: verify patient approval + B MFA + institution + scope + TTL
    CP->>AU: KEY_RELEASE_ALLOW/DENY
    CP->>K: one-time authorization(package,B,key version)
    K->>K: rewrap DEK for B Gateway public key
    K-->>BG: B Key Envelope, never plaintext DEK
    BG->>K: unwrap using B workload identity/private key protection
    BG->>BG: decrypt only after integrity verification
    BG->>AU: KEY_UNWRAP/DECRYPT result
    BG->>K: destroy transient handle after view/import

%% Revoked consent, expired/replayed Ticket, wrong institution/scope, blocked device,
%% failed integrity or stale key version => no authorization and no envelope.
%% ML-KEM hybrid wrapping is P1 crypto-agility, not an implemented claim.
